Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: read the NX30 Pro WAN MAC from a provisioned source

The pinned source reads the WAN MAC of the h3c,nx30pro board from the
pdt_data_1 partition and derives the LAN MAC from it. The 112M
partition contract of this device has no pdt_data_1 partition, because
that space is part of the larger UBI area, so on this layout the stock
code finds no MAC at all.

Take the WAN MAC from a provisioned file first, then from the factory
data area, and only then from the stock partition when a device still
carries it. The provisioned file /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac is written at
deployment time and is never part of the image, so no device MAC is
stored in this repository.

When no MAC is found the interfaces keep the addresses the boot loader
handed over instead of getting a derived wrong one, and the case is
logged.

The stock script also writes a derived Wi-Fi MAC into the Factory
partition when its first two bytes read 00-0c. This port drops that
write: the calibration partition stays read only, the vendor
provisioned Wi-Fi MAC is preserved, and the stock write together with
the real calibration data source stays unresolved until device testing
is separately authorized.

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
index ae85c00..dad3a9f 100755
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -249,12 +249,32 @@ mediatek_setup_macs()
 		label_mac=$lan_mac
 		;;
 	h3c,nx30pro)
-		wan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_ascii pdt_data_1 ethaddr)
-		lan_mac=$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 1)
-		if [ "$(mtk_factory_get_byte "Factory" 4 2)" = "00-0c" ]; then
-			local wifi_mac="$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 2)"
-			mtk_facrory_write_mac "Factory" 4 $wifi_mac
+		# The 112M partition contract has no pdt_data_1 partition, so the stock
+		# location of the WAN MAC is gone on this layout. Read the provisioned
+		# file first, then the factory data area, and only then the stock
+		# partition for a device that still carries it. The provisioned file
+		# is written at deployment time and is never part of the image, so no
+		# device MAC is stored in this repository.
+		if [ -f /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac ]; then
+			wan_mac="$(cat /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac)"
+		fi
+		if [ -z "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			wan_mac="$(mtd_get_mac_ascii Factory ethaddr)"
+		fi
+		if [ -z "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			wan_mac="$(mtd_get_mac_ascii pdt_data_1 ethaddr)"
+		fi
+		if [ -n "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			lan_mac=$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 1)
+		else
+			logger -t board.d -p user.warn \
+				"no WAN MAC for h3c,nx30pro, provision /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac"
 		fi
+		# The stock script writes a derived Wi-Fi MAC into the Factory
+		# partition when its first two bytes read 00-0c. This port keeps the
+		# calibration partition read only and leaves the vendor provisioned
+		# Wi-Fi MAC alone; the stock write and the calibration data source
+		# stay unresolved until device testing is authorized.
 		;;
 	*cmcc,a10* |\
 	*konka,komi-a31*)
